{"name":"Day Glow","hex":"#eadd82","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"},{"term":"glow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit heat and light without a flame.","To emit heat and light without a flame."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","A state of heat being emitted by a person or an animal's body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/1280px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut